# Production alerting — who gets told when production is broken (P0-6).
#
# First non-comment line is either an EMAIL ADDRESS or the word `off`.
# Editing this file on main runs .github/workflows/alerts.yml, which creates
# (or updates) an Azure Monitor action group routed to that address plus the
# alert rules below. `off` deletes all of them. Changing the address is an
# edit + push; no redeploy is involved.
#
# OPTIONAL extra lines (assessment 5-2 — one inbox, no paging, sev-1 and
# sev-2 on the same channel):
#
#   sms <country code> <number>     e.g.   sms 32 470123456
#   webhook <https url>             e.g.   webhook https://hooks.example/...
#
# When either is present a SECOND action group `clarion-alerts-sev1` is
# created carrying email + sms + webhook, and the SEVERITY-1 rules
# (clarion-backend-5xx, clarion-server-errors) route to it — production
# down pages a phone; a failed sync stays an email. Remove the lines to go
# back to email-only.
#
# Flood control (5-2): `clarion-failed-syncs` and `clarion-brute-force` now
# MUTE their actions for 4 hours after firing — one dead source or one
# scripted login burst produces one email, not one every 15 minutes into
# the inbox the outage mail lands in. The rule keeps evaluating; only the
# notification is muted.
#
# Every run also REPORTS whether an App Insights availability (web) test
# exists in the resource group (5-1). It does not create one — see the
# note at the bottom — but a run that finds none says so in its summary,
# every time, so "documented as create-it-in-the-portal" cannot quietly
# stay undone.
#
# Rules the workflow maintains:
#   clarion-backend-5xx        ≥10 5xx responses on the backend in 15 min
#   clarion-backend-restarts   container restarts on the backend app
#   clarion-worker-restarts    container restarts on the jobs-worker app
#   clarion-pg-cpu             Postgres flexible server CPU ≥ 90% (15 min avg)
#   clarion-pg-storage         Postgres flexible server storage ≥ 85%
#   clarion-server-errors      'request failed' lines (HTTP ≥500 in the app
#                              logs — the .ops/prod-logs `server-error`
#                              signature) ≥5 in 15 min
#   clarion-failed-syncs       any 'sync run failed' line (the load-bearing
#                              string SyncOrchestrator logs when a sync run is
#                              persisted as failed — and, since P0-6, as
#                              PARTIAL: the worker finished but one or more
#                              entities did not; the line carries partial:true)
#   clarion-brute-force        ≥10 'brute force limit hit' lines in 15 min —
#                              the brute limiters (per-IP and per-account,
#                              P1-2) log this exact string every time they
#                              refuse a request (middleware/rateLimitStore.ts bruteLimitHandler)
#   clarion-queue-depth        ≥3 'queue depth high' lines in 15 min — the
#                              queue-depth monitor (jobs/queueDepthMonitor.ts,
#                              P1-6) sweeps every minute and logs the string
#                              while a queue's WAITING count is at or above
#                              QUEUE_DEPTH_WARN (default 25), so 3+ lines
#                              means several minutes of sustained backlog,
#                              not a blip
#   clarion-stale-source       ≥1 'source stale' line in 15 min — the
#                              freshness monitor (jobs/freshnessMonitor.ts,
#                              7-1) sweeps hourly and logs the string for
#                              every scheduled source that has delivered no
#                              data within twice its own schedule's longest
#                              gap (+30 min, never under 2 h). The sync that
#                              never RAN — nothing in the run history says
#                              so, only the calendar. Muted 12 h.
#   clarion-sql-guard          ≥3 'sql guard refused' lines in 15 min — the
#                              read-query guard (utils/sqlGuard.ts) logs this
#                              string on every refusal, with tenant + user.
#                              Added 2026-09-05 after a bypass was found and
#                              fixed (assessment v2, P0-1): a tenant probing
#                              the guard must leave a trace. 3+ in 15 min is
#                              probing, one is a model slip.
#
# Deliberately NOT here (and why):
#   uptime probing   a continuous availability test wants an App Insights
#                    standard web test. Creating one via az from this
#                    workflow means an untestable ARM blob inside a control
#                    whose contract is "any rule that fails to create fails
#                    the run" — a bad trade against the working alert path.
#                    It is ONE resource with a guided form: create it in the
#                    portal (Application Insights → Availability → Add
#                    standard test, URL = the backend /api/ping), point its
#                    alert at the clarion-alerts action group, done in ~3
#                    minutes. The deploy gate + 5xx/restart alerts cover the
#                    broken-under-traffic case meanwhile; the web test adds
#                    the down-while-idle and ingress/DNS cases.
